bunit alpha</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">Translation initiation factor eIF-2B subunit beta</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">Translation initiation factor eIF-2B subunit delta</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">Translation initiation factor eIF-2B subunit epsilon</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">Translation initiation factor eIF-2B subunit gamma</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">Tubulin beta-4A chain</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">ABCD1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">ACOX1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">ADAR</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">ALDH3A2</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">ARSA</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">ASPA</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">CSF1R</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">CYP27A1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">DARS2</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">EARS2</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">EIF2B1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">EIF2B2</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">EIF2B3</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">EIF2B4</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">EIF2B5</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">FAM126A</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">FUCA1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">GALC</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">GBE1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">GFAP</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">GJA1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">GJC2</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">HEPACAM</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">HSD17B4</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">L2HGDH</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">LMNB1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">MLC1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX10</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX12</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX13</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX14</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX16</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX19</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX2</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX26</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX3</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX5</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PEX6</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PLP1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">POLR3A</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">POLR3B</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">PSAP</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">RNASEH2A</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">RNASEH2B</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">RNASEH2C</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">RNASET2</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">SAMHD1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">SCP2</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">SLC17A5</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">SOX10</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">SUMF1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">TREX1</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">TUBB4A</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">Leukodystrophy</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">Overview</Keyword></KeywordList><ContributionDate><Year>2014</Year><Month>2</Month><Day>6</Day></ContributionDate><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Bezman L, Moser AB, Raymond GV, Rinaldo P, Watkins PA, Smith KD, Kass NE, Moser HW. Adrenoleukodystrophy: incidence, new mutation rate, and results of extended family screening. Ann Neurol. 2001;49:512&#x2013;7.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">11310629</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Bonkowsky JL, Nelson C, Kingston JL, Filloux FM, Mundorff MB, Srivastava R. The burden of inherited leukodystrophies in children. Neurology. 2010;75:718&#x2013;25.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC2931652</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">20660364</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Eichler F, Grodd W, Grant E, Sessa M, Biffi A, Bley A, Kohlschuetter A, Loes DJ, Kraegeloh-Mann I. Metachromatic leukodystrophy: a scoring system for brain MR imaging observations. AJNR Am J Neuroradiol. 2009;30:1893&#x2013;7.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC7051299</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">19797797</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Heim P, Claussen M, Hoffmann B, Conzelmann E, G&#xe4;rtner J, Harzer K, Hunneman DH, K&#xf6;hler W, Kurlemann G, Kohlsch&#xfc;tter A. Leukodystrophy incidence in Germany. Am J Med Genet. 1997;71:475&#x2013;8.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">9286459</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Schiffmann R, van der Knaap MS. Invited article: an MRI-based approach to the diagnosis of white matter disorders. Neurology. 2009;72:750&#x2013;9.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC2677542</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">19237705</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>van der Knaap MS, Breiter SN, Naidu S, Hart AA, Valk J. Defining and categorizing leukoencephalopathies of unknown origin: MR imaging approach. Radiology. 1999;213:121&#x2013;33.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">10540652</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>van der Knaap MS, Valk J. <i>Magnetic Resonance of Myelination and Myelin Disorders</i>. Berlin, Germany: Springer. 2005.</Citation></Reference></ReferenceList></BookDocument><PubmedBookData><History><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="entrez"><Year>2014</Year><Month>2</Month><Day>6</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="medline"><Year>2014</Year><Month>2</Month><Day>6</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pubmed"><Year>2014</Year><Month>2</Month><Day>6</Day></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>ppublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24501781</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></PubmedBookData></PubmedBookArticle><PubmedArticle><MedlineCitation Status="MEDLINE" Owner="NLM" IndexingMethod="Manual"><PMID Version="1">21392394</PMID><DateCompleted><Year>2011</Year><Month>07</Month><Day>05</Day></DateCompleted><DateRevised><Year>2022</Year><Month>04</Month><Day>10</Day></DateRevised><Article PubModel="Electronic"><Journal><ISSN IssnType="Electronic">1750-1172</ISSN><JournalIssue CitedMedium="Internet"><Volume>6</Volume><PubDate><Year>2011</Year><Month>Mar</Month><Day>10</Day></PubDate></JournalIssue><Title>Orphanet journal of rare diseases</Title><ISOAbbreviation>Orphanet J Rare Dis</ISOAbbreviation></Journal><ArticleTitle>Autosomal recessive cerebellar ataxia caused by mutations in the PEX2 gene.</ArticleTitle><Pagination><StartPage>8</StartPage><MedlinePgn>8</MedlinePgn></Pagination><ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/1750-1172-6-8</ELocationID><Abstract><AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To expand the spectrum of genetic causes of autosomal recessive cerebellar ataxia (ARCA).</AbstractText><AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">Two brothers are described who developed progressive cerebellar ataxia at 3 1/2 and 18 years, respectively. After ruling out known common genetic causes of ARCA, analysis of blood peroxisomal markers strongly suggested a peroxisomal biogenesis disorder. Sequencing of candidate PEX genes revealed a homozygous c.865_866insA mutation in the PEX2 gene leading to a frameshift 17 codons upstream of the stop codon. PEX gene mutations usually result in a severe neurological phenotype (Zellweger spectrum disorders).</AbstractText><AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Genetic screening of PEX2 and other PEX genes involved in peroxisomal biogenesis is warranted in children and adults with ARCA.</AbstractText></Abstract><AuthorList CompleteYN="Y"><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Sevin</LastName><ForeName>Caroline</ForeName><Initials>C</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Pediatric Neurology and Endocrinology, H&#xf4;pital St Vincent de Paul, Paris, France. caroline.sevin@inserm.fr</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Ferdinandusse</LastName><ForeName>Sacha</ForeName><Initials>S</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Waterham</LastName><ForeName>Hans R</ForeName><Initials>HR</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Wanders</LastName><ForeName>Ronald J</ForeName><Initials>RJ</Initials></Author><Auth